---
source: crates/gough-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: o.out
---
Force recovery from a surviving node

Usage: gough primary force-recover [OPTIONS] --surviving-node <SURVIVING_NODE> --reason <REASON>

Options:
      --surviving-node <SURVIVING_NODE>
          Surviving node id
  -o, --output <FORMAT>
          Output format: table, json, yaml or jsonpath=<RFC 9535 expression> [default: table]
      --reason <REASON>
          Why recovery is forced (audit logged)
  -q, --quiet
          Suppress all output except errors
      --no-color
          Disable colored output
      --cluster <URL>
          Cluster API URL (env GOUGH_CLUSTER_URL); overrides the config file
      --context <NAME>
          Named context from the config file (env GOUGH_CURRENT_CONTEXT)
  -v, --verbose
          Log requests and diagnostics to stderr (tokens are masked)
      --ca-file <FILE>
          Extra PEM CA bundle to trust for the cluster's TLS certificate
  -h, --help
          Print help
